  {
    "question_id": "Q2.8",
    "class": 8,
    "subject": "history",
    "chapter_number": 2,
    "chapter_name": "from trade to territory",
    "question_type": "conceptual",
    "question_text": "In what way was the administration of the Company different from that of Indian rulers?",
    "question_latex": null,
    "mcq_options": [],
    "correct_option": null,
    "question_image": {
      "present": false,
      "description": null,
      "cloudinary_url": null,
      "latex_extracted": null,
      "source_page_number": null,
      "source_image_index": null,
      "ownership": "unknown"
    },
    "parts": [],
    "answer_text": "British territories were broadly divided into administrative units called Presidencies. There were three Presidencies like - Bengal, Madras & Bombay whereas under the Indian rulers administration was divided into four parts - District (Zila), Paragana, Tehsil and Villages. Each administrative unit was ruled by a Governor. The supreme head of the administration was the Governor-General, whereas under the Indian Administrative system the supreme head was King or Nawab. Warren Hastings introduced the new system of justice. Each district was to have two courts- civil & criminal court. The European District Collector presided over civil courts. The criminal courts were still under a Qazi and a Mufti. Under the Regulating Act of 1773, a new supreme court was established. The main figure in an Indian District was Collector. According to his title Collector, his main job was to collect the revenue and the taxes and maintain law & order in his district with the help of judges, police officers and darogas.",
    "answer_latex": null,
    "steps": [],
    "final_answer": "Thus, the administration of the Company was more centralized and structured compared to the fragmented system of Indian rulers.",
    "answer_image": {
      "present": false,
      "description": null,
      "cloudinary_url": null,
      "latex_extracted": null,
      "source_page_number": null,
      "source_image_index": null,
      "ownership": "unknown"
    },
    "difficulty_rating": 2,
    "difficulty_reasoning": "Requires understanding of administrative structures and their differences.",
